---
import Page from "../components/Page.astro";

const buildDate = new Date().toLocaleString("en-US", {
  dateStyle: "long",
});
---

<Page
  pageTitle="Now | Brad Azevedo"
  pageDescription="What’s Brad Azevedo up to these days?"
>
  <h1>Now</h1>

  <p class="subtle">
    Inspired by the “<a
      href="https://nownownow.com/about"
      rel="external nofollow">now page</a
    >” movement, these are some highlights of recent projects, accomplishments,
    and whatever else I might be working on.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <h2>2026</h2>

  <ol reversed>
    <li>
      I’m officially back on the hunt for my next role as a Design or Front-end
      Engineer, ideally somewhere in SF that really cares about craft in the
      UI/UX. If that sounds like your team, <a
        href="mailto:brad2k@gmail.com?subject=Howdy!"
        rel="external noopener">say hi</a
      > or take a look at my <a href="/resume/">resume</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Back home from three months in Australia, where my partner, James, played
      a stint with the Melbourne Symphony Orchestra. It was great to be back in
      one of my favorite cities — a place I was fortunate to live in for a
      couple of years — and we also had the opportunity to take a campervan trip
      to the Flinders Ranges and a side trip to Bali. It was a pretty solid way
      to close out my sabbatical.
    </li>
    <li>
      Launched <a
        href="https://tails.bradazevedo.com/"
        rel="external noopener"
        target="_blank">Tails</a
      >, my personal cocktail library. I’ve been getting into craft cocktails
      recently and struggled to catalog recipes I found, so I built Tails to
      keep track. It remains a work in progress that I’ll refine over time.
    </li>
    <li>
      Picked up a Google Project Management certificate — a low-stakes
      experiment to see if it’s something I’d like to fold into future roles.
    </li>
    <li>Passed my Instrument Ground Instructor exam!</li>
    <li>
      Implemented Style Dictionary on this site, which was…interesting. It was a
      fun exercise to see how it serves as the glue between Figma and the
      front-end, though it’s definitely overkill for this site.
    </li>
    <li>
      Re-launched <a href="/">www.bradazevedo.com</a> — this website! (I actually
      forgot I had one). The old one was mainly a hidden space for my CV and was built
      in Gatsby, but I rebuilt it in Astro with greater ambition this time, though
      it remains a work in progress.
    </li>
    <li>
      Launched <a
        href="https://thebeeline.bike/"
        rel="external noopener"
        target="_blank">The Beeline</a
      >, a site cataloging my favorite bike routes around San Francisco — equal
      parts sharing what I know as a cyclist and an excuse to try some newer web
      tech.
    </li>
    <li>
      Officially took partial ownership of a cutting-edge 1981 Cessna T182.
    </li>
    <li>Passed my Advanced Ground Instructor knowledge exam!</li>
    <li>
      Launched <a
        href="https://jamesbuttonoboe.com/"
        rel="external noopener"
        target="_blank">jamesbuttonoboe.com</a
      > — a website for my partner and brilliant oboist, James Button.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>2025</h2>

  <ol reversed>
    <li>
      Diving deep into all the latest and greatest in CSS: fluid type scales,
      powerful new selectors, container queries, theming, OKLCH, and more. Whew!
    </li>
    <li>
      Flew James and me to Portland, OR (<abbr title="Troutdale Airport"
        >KTTD</abbr
      >) — my longest flight yet, and the “long cross-country” required for the
      commercial certificate.
    </li>
    <li>
      Passed my Fundamentals of Instruction exam, the prerequisite for any FAA
      instructor certificate.
    </li>
    <li>
      Passed my Commercial Pilot knowledge exam. Now, onto the flight portion…
    </li>
    <li>
      Ate my first whole lobster in Portland, Maine. Alive, then boiled, then
      dismantled with an alarming number of tools. Messy, but entertaining.
    </li>
  </ol>
</Page>

<style>
  ol {
    list-style-type: disc;
  }
</style>
